    "narrative": "The Zurich Zebras enter today\u2019s slate with **Junior Caminero** serving as our anchor; his 70.79 efficiency score is the class of the roster, fueled by a favorable 4.46 xERA matchup against Sandy Alcantara and a significant boost from hitting in the two-hole. Close behind are **Pete Crow-Armstrong** (64.79) and **Casey Schmitt** (63.92). **Pete Crow-Armstrong** benefits heavily from a dynamic platoon edge (+14%) despite the risk of an elite holder behind the dish, while **Casey Schmitt** leverages an ideal park factor (+10%) and SP vulnerability to provide reliable production. Notably, **Luke Raley** (62.61) is a high-upside play today; his score is elevated by Walker Buehler\u2019s slow delivery, which provides a unique window to hunt stolen bases, a primary focus for our roster construction.\n\nDecision-making on the fringe remains tight, with **Chase Meidroth** (48.57) serving as the most difficult omission from our starting nine. **Chase Meidroth** was narrowly edged out by the superior platoon profiles of our middle infield, as the optimizer prioritized the specific matchup advantages held by **Caleb Durbin** and **Kazuma Okamoto**. We are proceeding with caution regarding the pending lineups; **Gary Sanchez**, **Dillon Dingler**, **Luke Raley**, **Casey Schmitt**, **Trea Turner**, **Caleb Durbin**, **Kazuma Okamoto**, **Yordan Alvarez**, **Pete Crow-Armstrong**, **Christian Yelich**, **Kyle Schwarber**, **Carson Benge**, and **Junior Caminero** all currently rely on projected spots that must be confirmed. Specifically, **Yordan Alvarez** faces a significant hurdle today against Jacob deGrom, whose elite status drops **Yordan Alvarez**\u2019s SP skill modifier by 19%. We are monitoring weather across all venues, as any late-breaking shifts could necessitate adjustments to our bench composition, which currently includes **Hyeseong Kim**, **Colt Keith**, and **Zac Veen**, the latter of whom remains sidelined in the minors.",
